# File layout

- File-scoped namespaces.
- One public type per file. File name = type name.
- Do not put dots in class file names (`Type.Part.cs`). Partials: `TypePart.cs` (PascalCase suffix, no dots). Keep EF `*.Designer.cs` only when the tool generates them.
- Place types under the feature folder that owns the context.
- Command `record` and handler may share a file only while both stay tiny; prefer separate files as soon as either grows.

```csharp
namespace Application.Commands.Pages;

public record CreatePageCommand(CreatePageRequest Request)
    : IRequest<CreatePageResponse>;
```
